Project Documentation Phase

The Project Documentation Phase is the stage where all important information about the project is recorded and organized for future reference.

Main Points:

Record Project Details – Document the project objectives, features, and requirements.
Explain System Design – Include diagrams, architecture, database design, and workflows.
Document Development – Record technologies, tools, coding methods, and implementation details.
Record Testing – Include test cases, results, errors found, and solutions.
Prepare User Guide – Explain how users can install, access, and use the project.
